<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore Dec industrial output down 0.3 pct on yr.</title>
<headline>Singapore Dec industrial output down 0.3 pct on yr.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's total manufacturing output fell by 0.3 percent in December compared to the same month the year before after falling 4.4 per cent in November, the Economic Development Board (EDB) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said in a statement cumulative growth for manufacturing in 1996 was 3.4 percent.</p>
<p>Table of Singapore's top 10 industries:</p>
<p>				    (pct change over previous year)</p>
<p>				    Dec 96	 Nov 96	  Oct 96</p>
<p>   *Total manufacturing	-0.3	   -4.4	    2.7</p>
<p>    Electronics		  -2.5	   -8.4	    4.9</p>
<p>    Fabricated Metals	  -7.9	  -11.3	   -2.6</p>
<p>    Transport Equipment	 8.9	   -5.5	   -0.8</p>
<p>    Machinery x-electronics  17.4	  -10.1	   -8.0</p>
<p>    Petroleum products	  5.8	    0.1	   -2.7</p>
<p>    Paints, pharmaceuticals  -2.3	   39.6	   -4.4</p>
<p>    Printing/publishing	-3.5	   -4.4	    2.2</p>
<p>    Industrial chems/gas	6.8	   41.2	   92.7</p>
<p>    Electrical machines	 1.7	   -3.0	    8.8</p>
<p>    Plastic products	  -21.6	  -23.9	   -6.2</p>
<p>* Total manufacturing output excludes rubber processing.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
